---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import site from '../../../site.config.json' with { type: 'json' };

const page = {
  url: '/about/gabriel-machuret/', title: 'Gabriel Machuret — Founder',
  seoTitle: 'Gabriel Machuret — Founder of Marine Diesel Engine Australia',
  seoTitleTag: 'Gabriel Machuret | Marine Diesel Engine Australia Founder',
  pageType: 'founder-profile', status: 'ready',
  author: 'Gabriel Machuret', authorType: 'Person',
  authorUrl: '/about/gabriel-machuret/', reviewer: null,
  needsReviewer: false, parent: '/about/', parentTitle: 'About us',
  schema: ['AboutPage', 'BreadcrumbList'], updated: '2026-10-02',
  indexable: true, blockers: [], faqs: [],
  headings: [
    { depth: 2, slug: 'marketing-and-publishing', text: 'Marketing and publishing' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'building-around-life', text: 'Building around the life I want' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'why-marine-diesel-engine', text: 'Why Marine Diesel Engine Australia' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'what-i-am-and-am-not', text: 'What I am—and what I am not' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'get-in-touch', text: 'Get in touch' },
  ],
  description: 'Meet Gabriel Machuret, founder of Marine Diesel Engine Australia and YouSail. Learn about his publishing career, books and sailing plans.',
  primaryKeyword: 'Gabriel Machuret founder', searchIntent: 'Navigational',
  extraSchema: [
    {
      '@type': 'ProfilePage',
      '@id': `${site.domain}/about/gabriel-machuret/#profile`,
      mainEntity: { '@id': `${site.domain}/about/gabriel-machuret/#person` },
      dateModified: '2026-10-02',
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Person',
      '@id': `${site.domain}/about/gabriel-machuret/#person`,
      name: 'Gabriel Machuret',
      url: `${site.domain}/about/gabriel-machuret/`,
      jobTitle: 'Founder and publisher',
      description: 'Founder of Marine Diesel Engine Australia and YouSail; marketer, author and digital publisher.',
      sameAs: ['https://yousail.com.au/'],
      worksFor: { '@id': `${site.domain}/#publisher` },
    },
  ],
};
---
<Page page={page}>
  <header class="founder-profile-hero">
    <div class="founder-monogram founder-monogram--large" aria-hidden="true">GM</div>
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Founder and publisher</p>
      <h1>Gabriel Machuret</h1>
      <p>
        I’m Gabriel, the creator of Marine Diesel Engine Australia and
        <a href="https://yousail.com.au/" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouSail</a>.
        I build useful websites around the life I want to live. Right now, that
        life is sailing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <h2 id="marketing-and-publishing">Marketing and publishing</h2>
  <p>
    My background is marketing. I have spent more than a decade in search
    engine optimisation and app store optimisation, and I was one of the first
    people to treat ASO as its own discipline. In 2013, I launched the first
    ASO course on Udemy, then wrote <em>The ASO Bible</em> and <em>ASO Ninja</em>.
    More than 10,000 students have been through my courses.
  </p>
  <p>
    Along the way I ran a marketing agency and worked with companies including
    Red Bull, Disney, EA Games, FreshBooks, PBS and Xerox. I have helped more
    than 500 developers and app companies get found, and spoken at conferences
    in London, Singapore, China and Thailand. I also acquired the ASO company
    Appmind, which was later acquired by Mobile Action, where I stayed on as a
    consultant and ambassador.
  </p>
  <p>
    Not everything I write is about marketing. <em>Zero Excuses</em> is my book
    about living a beautiful life. <em>The Lazy Bastard</em> is a productivity
    guide for procrastinators.
  </p>

  <h2 id="building-around-life">Building around the life I want</h2>
  <p>
    I have a habit: I build websites around the life I want to live. When I
    worked as a diving instructor, I built diving websites. Now it is sailing.
  </p>
  <p>
    My partner Kristy and I are working towards buying a yacht, moving aboard
    and sailing Australia and the Pacific. We are still learning, taking
    courses, spending time on boats and asking a lot of questions. That process
    has already produced a network of useful sailing projects, including Top
    Marinas, Sailing Schools, Sailing Courses, Sailing Clubs, Top Charters and
    Buy Sails.
  </p>

  <h2 id="why-marine-diesel-engine">Why Marine Diesel Engine Australia</h2>
  <p>
    Prepare for life aboard and engine questions arrive quickly. What does a
    warning sign mean? Which maintenance jobs belong on the calendar? How do
    two engines really compare? What should a repower quote include? The answers
    live in many different places and are often written for technicians rather
    than owners.
  </p>
  <p>
    So I did what I know how to do: collect information, organise it around real
    questions and make it easier to use. Marine Diesel Engine Australia is not
    a substitute for a workshop manual or mechanic. It is a better starting
    point for understanding the issue and having a more informed conversation
    with the right professional.
  </p>

  <aside class="founder-quote">
    <p>“Moving onto a yacht is me running out of excuses.”</p>
  </aside>

  <h2 id="what-i-am-and-am-not">What I am—and what I am not</h2>
  <p>
    I am not a marine mechanic, naval architect or expert sailor, and I have not
    worked on every engine described here. My expertise is research, digital
    publishing and making complex information easier to navigate. Technical
    claims should come from identifiable primary sources, and qualified review
    should be named rather than implied.
  </p>
  <p>
    That distinction matters. Advice about an engine can be incomplete or
    wrong, including advice published here. Always check the manual for the
    exact model and installation, and use a qualified marine mechanic for
    diagnosis, safety-critical work and decisions that could damage the vessel
    or put people at risk.
  </p>

  <h2 id="get-in-touch">Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    I’m based in Merimbula on the NSW South Coast. If you maintain marine
    engines, represent a marine brand, have evidence that can improve a guide or
    simply want to talk boats, email me at
    <a href="mailto:gabriel@yousail.com.au">gabriel@yousail.com.au</a>.
  </p>
  <p class="about-close">
    Follow the wider sailing story at
    <a href="https://yousail.com.au/" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouSail.com.au <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>.
  </p>
</Page>
